            You can wear running shoes for pickleball, especially while you are trying the game, but they are built for the wrong direction. Their tall, soft heels, light uppers and forward-biased outsoles make lateral cuts less stable than they would be in a court shoe.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Once you play regularly, switch to a pickleball, tennis or indoor court shoe that fits well and suits your surface. It is an inexpensive change that gives you a lower, more stable base and better grip for the side-to-side movement that makes up most of the game.
